# Big Idea 4: Humans Are Responsible for How AI Is Used

By the end of Thinking Critically About AI, students move beyond simply analyzing AI systems and toward making their own evidence-based judgments about how humans should use AI responsibly.

## What Students Learn

<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:14px; margin:25px 0px;">

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      Humans Remain Accountable
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students explore why people, not AI systems, are ultimately responsible for decisions and consequences.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      Evidence Supports Conclusions
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students use examples, testing, and observations from across the unit to justify their positions about responsible AI use.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div style="background-color:#F5F7F8; padding:18px; border-radius:10px; width:32%; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
      Responsible Use is Nuanced
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Students synthesize multiple perspectives and recognize that responsible AI use often depends on context and judgment.
    </p>
  </div>

</div>

A major instructional goal of this section of the unit is helping students develop evidence-based positions rather than relying on simple reactions or assumptions about AI.

## Across the Unit

As students approach the end of the unit, they begin synthesizing ideas from earlier investigations into broader conclusions about responsibility and AI use.

* **Lesson 9** asks students to revise and strengthen their Generate and Judge Guide using evidence and feedback
* **Lesson 10** challenges students to defend positions about how involved humans should be when using AI systems
* Throughout the project, students repeatedly revisit and refine their own recommendations for responsible AI use

Across these lessons, students begin recognizing that thoughtful AI use requires ongoing human judgment, reflection, and accountability.

